<h2 id=3D"17">Smaji Glyph Path</h2>
<div class=3D"outline-text-2" id=3D"text-17">
<p>
Archive: <a href=3D"https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-smaji-glyph-path/18446/=
1">https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-smaji-glyph-path/18446/1</a>
</p>
</div>
<div id=3D"outline-container-org425ec77" class=3D"outline-3">
<h3 id=3D"org425ec77">ZAN DoYe announced</h3>
<div class=3D"outline-text-3" id=3D"text-org425ec77">
<p>
<a href=3D"https://github.com/smaji-org/smaji_glyph_path">Smaji Glyph Path<=
/a>
</p>

<p>
An OCaml library for manipulation of font glyph outlines. It provides a sui=
te of tools for analyzing, transforming, composing, and converting glyph pa=
ths between different formats.
</p>

<p>
This library supports two primary path description standards:
</p>

<ol class=3D"org-ol">
<li>SVG Path: Supports <code>&lt;path&gt;</code> element (including its <co=
de>d</code> attribute) and optional <code>&lt;g&gt;</code> element as conta=
iners.</li>
<li>Glif Format: Supports the data used to describe glyph outlines in the U=
nified Font Object (UFO) format.</li>
</ol>

<p>
It has published on opam, so it can be installed easily by <code>opam insta=
ll smaji_glyph_path</code>
</p>

<p>
And here are <a href=3D"https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/smaji-glyph-path-two-us=
ecases-smaji-outline-description-and-smaji-stroke-description/18447">two us=
e case samples</a>
</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
